// useWordUnscrambler.js for the combined loading logic.
// Stored as a single newline-delimited string rather than an array of
// separate quoted elements -- a single large string literal is one AST
// node for the bundler to parse, whereas millions of individual array
// elements each become their own node, which crashed the production
// build with an out-of-memory error even at an 8GB heap limit.
// Cleaned (25 Aug): removed 3,168 vulgar word forms (0.11% of the
// dictionary) found during a follow-up contamination check. Unlike the
// other 7 languages, Polish had no foreign-name/brand contamination risk
// (built from a legitimate curated Hunspell source, not scraped
// subtitles) -- the issue here was different: the source Hunspell
// dictionary legitimately includes crude vocabulary as real headwords
// (same as most spell-checkers do), and the full grammatical expansion
// then multiplied each one across all its conjugated/declined forms. An
// initial substring-based check wrongly flagged thousands of innocent
// words (e.g. NASLUCHUJESZ, "you listen", coincidentally contains a
// vulgar-looking substring); the corrected method only flagged words
// genuinely derived from confirmed vulgar headwords, verified by
// re-running those headwords through the same Hunspell affix expansion
// the whole dictionary was built with.
